🗄️ MEMORY & RAM
---------------
Mnemonic    Operands      Format            Description
--------    --------      ------            -----------
--Memory access need the 17th bit to be on, up to the 16th bit is the address, the 17th is the ram/rom bit
LD          RA, RB        LD Rn, Rn         Load RAM[RA] into RB
ST          RA, RB        ST Rn, Rn         Store RB into RAM[RA]
DATA        RB, .BYTE     DATA Rn, 0xNN     Load next byte into RB
ALD         RA, RB        ALD Rn, Rn        Load from array RA and index RB to R0
AST         RA, RB        AST Rn, Rn        Store R0 into array RA and index RB
CPY         RA, RB        CPY Rn, Rn        Copy RA to RB

🔁 FLOW CONTROL
---------------
Mnemonic    Operands      Format            Description
--------    --------      ------            -----------
JMRB        RB            JMRB Rn           Jump to address in RB
RJF         FLAGS         RJF CANZ          Relative jump if flags are set  
RJNF        FLAGS         RJNF CANZ         Relative jump if flags NOT set 
RJMP        .BYTE         RJMP .BYTE        Relative jump to next byte
CLF         (none)        CLF               Clear flags
HALT        (none)        HALT              Halt CPU

🧰 STACK OPERATIONS
-------------------
Mnemonic    Operands      Format             Description
--------    --------      ------             -----------
STK         PUSH, Rn      STK PUSH, Rn       Push Rn to stack
STK         POP, Rn       STK POP, Rn        Pop stack to Rn
STK         CALLF, Rn     STK CALLF          Call frame
STK         RETF, Rn      STK RETF           Return frame
STK         SET, Rn       STK SET, Rn        Stack set: Stack[Rn] = R0
STK         GET, Rn       STK GET, Rn        Stack get: R0 = Stack[Rn]

🔌 PERIPHERAL I/O
-----------------
Mnemonic    Operands        Format                Description
--------    --------        ------                -----------
COMM        INDATA, Rn      COMM INDATA, Rn       Peripheral input → Rn
COMM        INADDR, Rn      COMM INADDR, Rn       Peripheral address input(not used really)
COMM        OUTDATA, Rn     COMM OUTDATA, Rn      Peripheral output ← Rn
COMM        OUTADDR, Rn     COMM OUTADDR, Rn      Peripheral address output
ADDR        Rn              ADDR Rn               Load PC/IAR into Rn